Target: Meizu 21 Note, 5.15.119-android13-8-g6ff5097ee32a-ab1764665171 (qcom,kalama).
That kernel has CONFIG_MACVLAN=n, CONFIG_IP6_NF_NAT=n and
CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_ADDRTYPE=n. All three units are ordinary mainline
modules that the vendor build simply omits.

IPv6 NAT only needs the x_tables template: CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_MASQUERADE=y
compiles xt_MASQUERADE, which registers NFPROTO_IPV6 as well as NFPROTO_IPV4 in
5.15, and CONFIG_NF_NAT=y provides nf_nat_masquerade_ipv6. There is no separate
ip6t_MASQUERADE.c in this release. CONFIG_NF_TABLES is not set, so no nftables
unit is added here.

xt_addrtype is what Docker's iptables rules and -m addrtype setups need. The
device has CONFIG_IP6_NF_IPTABLES=y and the IPv6 helpers resolve, so the unit is
compiled with -DCONFIG_IP6_NF_IPTABLES=1 to keep the IPv6 match and its family
registration; the upstream file guards all of that behind that option.

The upstream files retain their original license notices. The local changes are:
- Replace the per-file module_init/module_exit entries with ds_nf_init_net515_* /
  ds_nf_exit_net515_* wrappers so one module can own all units and roll back in
  reverse order. Module metadata moved to main.c; the rtnl link and xtables aliases
  are kept.
- Build with -DCONFIG_MACVLAN=1 so include/linux/if_macvlan.h provides the inlined
  accessors instead of the CONFIG_MACVLAN-less BUG() stubs, and with
  -DCONFIG_IP6_NF_IPTABLES=1 so xt_addrtype keeps its IPv6 match.
- Restrict loading to the recorded device release or a 5.15.x linux,dummy-virt VM.

Nothing else is changed. Each unit is the ordinary mainline module: macvlan
registers its rtnl link kind and netdevice notifier, ip6table_nat registers an
empty IPv6 "nat" table template, xt_addrtype registers its matches. Module
initialization installs no rules and creates no links.

Cross-check: the third-party IPSET_LKM release v2.5 ships an ip6table_nat.ko and
xt_addrtype.ko built for 5.15.202 whose imported symbols are exactly the ones used
here, and every one of them is present on the target device.

Regression entry point: tests/vm/run-net515.sh (requires a VM image with iproute2,
iptables-legacy and ip6tables; see docs/meizu21note-net-extras.md).
